    "created_at": "2017-10-01T20:58:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-01T20:58:15Z",
    "body": "> Note, backslashes are not considered to be \"valid\", only \"accepted\"\r\n\r\nBut for a user that's effectively the same thing. The parser eats them and treats the string as if it was a valid URL.\r\n\r\nIt helped me understand that your spec says this is a fine URL. As you know, I protest against this (as well). Thanks for clarifying!",
